# Line endings for the Android project.
#
# This repository is cloned on Windows with autocrlf=true and built from WSL,
# and three of the files here break if the wrong one arrives.
#
#   gradlew          runs under sh. A CRLF shebang line gives
#                    "/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter", which is the single most
#                    reported Gradle-wrapper failure there is.
#   *.sh             same reason - see android/tools/make-icons.sh.
#   gradlew.bat      the opposite: cmd.exe wants CRLF, and Gradle generates it
#                    that way. Pinned so a checkout on a Linux box cannot
#                    normalise it to LF and quietly break the Windows launcher.
#   *.jar            binary. Git detects this on its own; the rule is here
#                    because a filtered wrapper jar is an unrunnable build with
#                    nothing in the diff to show why.
#
# See the repository-root .gitattributes for the same reasoning applied to the
# vendored typefaces.

gradlew      text eol=lf
*.sh         text eol=lf
gradlew.bat  text eol=crlf
*.jar        binary
*.png        binary
